    "4": {
      "uid": 4,
      "key": [
        "Maadteraahka",
        "Prayer Song II",
        "Hymns of the Far North"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Naberius: Maadteraahka",
      "content": "The Frostmoon Scions' hymn praises her as the mother of gods and mortals, revered from Hyperborea to Sal Vindagnyr, protector of women in childbirth and mother of the waters. In the old rite, a pinch of sea salt was offered at the sacred stone at a birth and the newborn bathed in warm water infused with Winter Icelea; Aila, the first Moonchanter, abolished the ritual five centuries ago.",
      "constant": false,
